/-!
# The integral roots of type E8 and their reflections

This file enumerates the 240 roots of type `E8` in the lattices used by the pinned simply
connected root datum of `TauCeti.LinearAlgebra.RootSystem.SimplyConnectedRootDatum.E8.Datum`, and
tabulates reflection in each of them. Coroots are expressed in the simple-coroot basis and roots in
the fundamental-weight basis. Both tables are indexed by the same `Fin 240`: the first eight
entries of the root table are the Bourbaki simple roots and the first eight entries of the coroot
table are the corresponding simple coroots. The remaining positive entries are ordered by height,
and the last 120 entries are the negatives of the first 120.

The enumeration is the root-data input for Layer 6 of the root-systems roadmap. It follows
Bourbaki, *Lie Groups and Lie Algebras, Chapters 4--6*, Plate VII.

## The two tables are one

Because `E8` is simply laced, a root and its coroot have the same simple-root coordinates, so the
stored coroot table determines both: if a coroot has coordinates `c`, then the root has coordinates
`⟨β, αⱼ^∨⟩ = ∑ i, cᵢ ⟨αᵢ, αⱼ^∨⟩`, that is, the Cartan-matrix image of `c`. That relation is
`TauCeti.DynkinType.e8Root_eq_mulVec`, and it is what makes reflection in the roots the image of
reflection in the coroots under a linear map rather than a second table.

## The reflections

Reflection is tabulated as a permutation of the root indices, and the table is cut down twice.
Reflection in a root and in its negative are the same map, so only the 120 positive roots index a
row; and reflection carries the negative of a root to the negative of its image, so only the 120
positive roots index a column, the remaining values being read off through the index involution
that exchanges the two halves. What is left is checked entry by entry against the stored
coordinates by the kernel, in `e8ReflectionTable_coroot`, so no entry of the table is taken on
trust. Reflection and the table both live here because that check has to unfold the stored
coordinates.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.DynkinType.e8Coroot` and `TauCeti.DynkinType.e8Root`: the coroot coordinate embedding
  and the root embedding derived from it by the Cartan-matrix map.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.e8SimpleIndex`: the first eight root indices, the Bourbaki-numbered simple
  roots.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.e8ReflectionPerm`: reflection in a root, as a permutation of the root indices.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.DynkinType.root_e8SimpleIndex` and `TauCeti.DynkinType.coroot_e8SimpleIndex`: the `i`-th
  simple root is the `i`-th row of `CartanMatrix.E₈` and the `i`-th simple coroot is
  `Pi.single i 1`, which is what pins the two lattices as the weight and the coroot lattice.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.e8Root_eq_mulVec`: the root coordinates are the Cartan-matrix image of the
  coroot coordinates.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.e8ReflectionPerm_root` and `TauCeti.DynkinType.e8ReflectionPerm_coroot`: the
  tabulated permutation is reflection on both tables.
-/

